1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sogneprest i Nes, Hedmark.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Ole was born in 1674.[1] He was a chaplain ("kapellan") at Nes, Hedmark, 1701-1706 and a parish priest ("sogneprest") at Nes, Hedmark, 1706-1744.[2] He passed away about 1744. Here is a picture of Ole.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT ↑ Nes prestekontor, Hedmark, SAH/PREST-020/L/La/L0001: Klokkerbok nr. 1, 1663-1784, s. 10-11
2 CONT ↑ Norsk prestehistorie – Hedemarken og Østerdalen prosti
2 CONT See also:
2 CONT
2 CONT Totens bygdebok. 3. Oslo, 1968, p. 589. Available to Norwegian IPs at Nasjonalbiblioteket
