1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nordahl Johan Brun
2 CONT ON 10.11.2020 BY OLGA MEDVEDEVAIN БЕЗ РУБРИКИ
2 CONT Nordahl Johan Brun (Chinese name 彭恩 Peng En) was born on 16 February 1867 in Christiania (Oslo), Norway. His father, Hans Salvesen Brun, was a well-known Norwegian actor and singer. Among his ancestors was the Bishop of Bergen, Jo
2 CONC han Nordahl Brun (1745–1816), a prominent clergyman and poet.
2 CONT
2 CONT Like many young men of his generation, Nordahl Johan Brun went to sea. He eventually made his way to China, and in August 1896 he entered the Marine Department of the Chinese Maritime Customs Service as a Lightkeeper in Shanghai. 
2 CONC The Marine Department, established in 1868, was responsible for improving approaches to the ports and facilitating navigation along the Chinese seaboard. Its staff were engaged in harbour and waterway management, as well as meteor
2 CONC ological observations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Brun’s service in the Customs was relatively brief. In February 1899, after approximately two and a half years, he resigned, holding the position of Second Lightship Mate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He subsequently continued his maritime career and later worked as a ship captain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nordahl Johan Brun died in 1925 in New York, United States. He was married to Augusta Gran from Askøy. The couple had a daughter, Bergliot, who later became an actress in Norway.
