1 NOTE {geni:about_me} JOHANN LORENTZ CARSTENS, ennobled as CASTENSCHIOLD J.L. Carstens was a Danish Creole born on St. Thomas. At the age of 16 he inherited two plantations. In 1728 he married his great love Jacoba von Holten, also a Cr
2 CONC eole. She gave her name to his ship Vrou Jacoba, which sailed in the Lübeck trade. As the name shows, Dutch was the everyday language for Euro-­‐Creoles on St. Thomas – including those of Danish origin. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 4.  Jacoba von Holten was born in about 1705 and was baptized on 29 December 1705 in the Lutheran Church, St. Thomas. Claudi van Beverhoudt’s wife [Anna, b. Martens] held the girl at the baptism.  The witnesses were Wolf Sigismund
2 CONC  and Jens Rasmussen. ( Lutheran Church, St. Thomas, Church Book, 1691-1795, f. 44, Baptisms) 	Jacoba von Holten was married in 1728 to Johan Lorentz Carstens, who was born on 18 May 1705.  (Herluf Nielsen, editor, “J. L. Carstens:
2 CONC  En Almindelig Beskrivelse om All de Danske, Americanske eller West-Jndiske Ey-Lande,” Danske Magazin, 8 set, vol. 3/22 (1967-1970), f. 173.)
2 CONT
2 CONT -------
2 CONT Danske i Amerika. 2 Bd. Minneapolis og Chicago, 1908 (D7). Har uddrag i kopi af mikrofiche fra SB samt kopi af siderne 39-45 + s. 385-397 i bd. 1. samt indholdsfortegnelse i bd. 2.  Stammoder til Castenschiolderne. Danske i Amerik
2 CONC a giver fødselsåret 1702, men E. Jensen giver præcis dato i 1704.  4 of their children (Jørgen, barn child, Margaretha and Johannes) born 1730, 1732, 1733, and 1747 respectively, all died young. Købte 1748 Hørbygaard og Gods af v.
2 CONC  d. Lühe for 18,250 RdI. og 100 Ducater. Hørbygaard har fra den Tid af været i Castenskjoldernes Besiddelse, medens Knabstrup solgtes 1764 for 50,000 Rdl.
